      "response": "## Investigation report\n\nCitation integrity checked against saved evidence. Human review is required to assess the findings.\n\n### 1. Docs · Low\n\nThe snippet imports the Streamlit library as the alias \\`st\\`\\.\n\nSource: User supplied reproduction code · user\\_code · ev\\_8345d14f4d0f57b572a095104cda4fbb\n\n> import streamlit as st\n> \n> @st\\.cache\\_data\n> def load\\_rows\\(\\):\n>     return \\[1, 2, 3\\]\n> \n> st\\.write\\(load\\_rows\\(\\)\\)\n\n### 2. Correctness · Low\n\nThe function \\`load\\_rows\\` is decorated with \\`@st\\.cache\\_data\\` and returns the list \\`\\[1, 2, 3\\]\\`\\.\n\nSource: User supplied reproduction code · user\\_code · ev\\_8345d14f4d0f57b572a095104cda4fbb\n\n> import streamlit as st\n> \n> @st\\.cache\\_data\n> def load\\_rows\\(\\):\n>     return \\[1, 2, 3\\]\n> \n> st\\.write\\(load\\_rows\\(\\)\\)\n\n### 3. Correctness · Low\n\n\\`st\\.write\\(load\\_rows\\(\\)\\)\\` is called, which will display the list \\`\\[1, 2, 3\\]\\` in the Streamlit app\\.\n\nSource: User supplied reproduction code · user\\_code · ev\\_8345d14f4d0f57b572a095104cda4fbb\n\n> import streamlit as st\n> \n> @st\\.cache\\_data\n> def load\\_rows\\(\\):\n>     return \\[1, 2, 3\\]\n> \n> st\\.write\\(load\\_rows\\(\\)\\)\n\n### Proposed next steps\n\n- Verify that the use of \\`@st\\.cache\\_data\\` is appropriate for this static list and that caching does not unintentionally hide changes if the function implementation is later modified\\.\n",
